{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>There</b> — for the shipmen tell us of great creatures they have seen within the sea." "<b>Leviathan</b> — a name for every great fish like it, or it is a name for every known species, and upon it the verse turns back to the sea, for all fish are food for it, and it is not food."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 104, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:38:15.872145808Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}